[{:adr/consequences "{:isekai_network_unblocked \"the specific compile-and-run blocker\\n                              isekai-network's README documented all\\n                              session is closed -- real execution, real\\n                              pixel-verified rendering, both backends\\n                              deterministic\", :third_kamiclj_gap_closed \"kotoba-lang/engine now has both halves closed\\n                              (semantic compile + byte emission); the\\n                              previously-undocumented host-runtime gap\\n                              (kami-script-runtime's permanent scope\\n                              exclusion) now has an owner\", :genre_base_systems_downstream \"kami-genre-base-systems (a separate,\\n                                   parallel initiative this session) can\\n                                   now, as real follow-up, actually\\n                                   WASM-compile + run its systems through\\n                                   this same pipeline -- not attempted in\\n                                   this ADR's scope, a legitimate next step\", :naming_debt \"one open naming question (kami-script-runtime-rs) is\\n                explicitly deferred, not silently accepted as final\"}", :adr/authoritative_for ["kotoba.engine-clj.wasm-bytes (kotoba-lang/engine, PR #1) is the byte-emission\n    step that closes the gap between kotoba.engine-clj's Module IR (semantic\n    compile, already-ported from deleted Rust codegen.rs) and real loadable\n    .wasm bytes -- ported 1:1 from the deleted Rust codegen.rs::compile\n    (kami-engine@a8368f9c0d784dbc9d11e8fa8f407aa95c7ce4fa:kami-engine-clj/src/codegen.rs)" "PR #2 fixed a real semantic bug PR #1 introduced (:f32-const encoded the\n    raw Clojure float literal instead of its num/f32-bits IEEE-754 bit\n    pattern) -- found only by kami-script-runtime-rs's real tick-loop\n    execution, not by wasm-tools validate (structurally valid, semantically\n    wrong -- any 4 bytes are valid IEEE-754)" "kotoba-lang/kami-script-runtime-rs is a new repo hosting the WASM HOST\n    substrate (wasmtime + wasmi backends, 14 host-import bindings, entity\n    store) recovered 1:1 from kami-engine's deleted\n    kami-script-runtime/src/lib.rs -- this Rust substrate was ALWAYS\n    classified :stay-Rust-substrate in ADR-2607010930's original ledger but\n    was accidentally swept into the wholesale kami-engine Rust-workspace\n    deletion; kotoba-lang/kami-script-runtime (the CLJC-scoped repo) only\n    ported the genuinely-portable input_map.rs submodule and explicitly,\n    permanently excludes the host substrate from its own scope -- this ADR\n    is the missing repo that closes that gap" "isekai-network's real games/01-netsurvivors/logic.clj compiles through\n    the full pipeline end-to-end and was verified actually running: entity\n    count grows via spawn, the beat-gated bonus mechanic fires, pixel-level\n    on-screen colour verification (via a real render-to-texture screenshot\n    capture) confirms shiro-pico/ghost accent colours match\n    character-design-spec.json's canonical palette after accounting for the\n    shader's glow-brightening + sRGB-encode pipeline"], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "kotoba-lang-clj-wgsl-runtime-closure", :adr/related ["CLAUDE.md" "90-docs/adr/2607010930-clj-wgsl-migration.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607023200-isekai-network-standalone-repo.edn" "manifest/repos.edn" "kotoba-lang/engine PR #1, PR #2 (both merged)" "kotoba-lang/kami-script-runtime-rs (new repo)" "gftdcojp/isekai-network"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607031700-kotoba-lang-engine-wasm-emission-and-host-runtime", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-03", :adr/body "# ADR 2607031700: kotoba-lang/engine WASM byte-emission + kotoba-lang/kami-script-runtime-rs (the recovered WASM host substrate)\n\n## Status\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\n`gftdcojp/isekai-network` (Ghost Hacker: Shiro & Pico) had a real,\nEDN-validated, proven-vocabulary-checked `games/01-netsurvivors/logic.clj`\nsince early this session, but no way to verify it actually ran.\n`kami-engine-clj` (the compiler `kami-engine`'s CLAUDE.md documented) turned\nout to have been deleted upstream (`kotoba-lang/kotoba` PR #259) as part of\nADR-2607010930's clj-wgsl migration. Its CLJC replacement — found under the\ndifferently-named `kotoba-lang/engine`, not something literally called\n`kamiclj` — compiled `logic.clj` to a Module IR successfully, but the IR was\na data structure, not loadable `.wasm` bytes. Even with bytes, nothing\nexisted to actually load and execute them with real host-import behaviour:\n`kotoba-lang/kami-script-runtime` (the CLJC-scoped repo) explicitly,\npermanently excludes the Rust WASM-host substrate from its own scope.\n\n## Decision\n\n### Byte emission: `kotoba.engine-clj.wasm-bytes` (kotoba-lang/engine, PR #1)\n\nA 1:1 port of the deleted Rust `codegen.rs::compile`'s section assembly\n(type/import/function/memory/global/export/code/data, same order, same\n`cabi_realloc` bump-allocator special case), recovered read-only from\n`kami-engine`'s git history at the same pin `codegen.cljc` itself was\nrecovered from. Verified with `wasm-tools validate` (independent external\nvalidator) and `wasmtime run --invoke` (real execution, not just structural\nvalidity), 51 tests / 213 assertions.\n\n**A real bug was found and fixed (PR #2)**: `:f32-const` was missing the\n`num/f32-bits` conversion, discovered only by `kami-script-runtime-rs`'s\nreal tick-loop execution — ghosts spawned via a `def`-bound constant moved\ncorrectly; ghosts using an inline `f32` literal in the same `cond` sat at a\nNaN position forever. `wasm-tools validate` never caught it because any 4\nbytes are structurally valid IEEE-754. Fixed with 2 new regression tests\nthat decode the emitted bytes back via an independent `ByteBuffer` read.\n\n### Host runtime: new repo `kotoba-lang/kami-script-runtime-rs`\n\nThe deleted Rust `kami-script-runtime/src/lib.rs` (2042 lines) was ALWAYS\nclassified `:stay-Rust-substrate` in ADR-2607010930's original ledger, but\nwas accidentally swept into the wholesale `kami-engine` Rust-workspace\ndeletion. `kotoba-lang/kami-script-runtime`'s CLJC port only restored the\ngenuinely-portable `input_map.rs` submodule and states its host-runtime\nexclusion in absolute terms (\"permanent scope exclusion, not a TODO\").\n`kotoba-lang/kami-script-runtime-rs` is the missing repo that closes this\ngap: wasmtime (JIT) + wasmi (no-JIT) dual backends, one binding codebase, 14\nhost-import implementations recovered 1:1 from the deleted `lib.rs`, a\nhand-rolled `HashMap`-based entity store (not `hecs` — disclosed\nsimplification). Render/audio/physics host-imports are NOT implemented\nbecause isekai-network's actual compiled module declares none — confirmed\nempirically, not assumed, matching the original pre-deletion Rust's own\nno-op status for those bindings.\n\n**Verified, not just \"it compiled\"**: a wasmi/wasmtime parity test runs\nisekai-network's real compiled module through both backends for 200 ticks\nand asserts bit-for-bit identical position/velocity/tag/count state — the\ngolden-frame determinism contract ADR-2607010930's original design called\nfor. `src/bin/kami_clj_play.rs` reuses the deleted original's wgpu\nrendering code, replaced its in-process `hecs`+CLJ-compile `Game` struct\nwith a thin `KamiHost` wrapper loading a pre-compiled `game.wasm`, plus a\nhand-rolled `scene.edn` parser scoped to `author.clj`'s known flat output\nshape. Confirmed running: a real window, sustained ~60fps for 720 frames,\nisekai-network's `game.wasm` executing live (entity count 5→21 via spawn,\nbeat-spark bonus firing), and pixel-level colour verification via a real\nrender-to-texture screenshot capture — Shiro's hood-white near-exact match,\nteal/lime eye accents consistent with the shader's glow-brightening + sRGB\nencode once that two-step colour pipeline was correctly accounted for\n(documented directly in the fragment shader source as a comment, so future\nverification work doesn't repeat the naive-hex-comparison gap the first\npass hit).\n\n### Naming: one open question, deliberately not resolved unilaterally\n\n`kami-script-runtime-rs`'s own README already flagged that no established\n`kotoba-lang` naming convention was found for \"Rust substrate host paired\nwith an almost-same-named CLJC sibling repo.\" This ADR does not rename the\nalready-public, manifest-registered, actively-depended-on repo — that's a\ndisruptive decision left to the project owner. Separately, `kami-genre-base-\nsystems`' `games/<genre>/` layout was checked against `kami-clj-play/games/`\nand found consistent (no naming gap there); whether individual genre\nsystems should eventually graduate to separate `kami-app-{genre}` crates\nper `ARCHITECTURE.md`'s convention is a real open question, deliberately\nleft unresolved since these are base/foundation prototypes, not\ncrate-worthy shipped games.\n\n### Library reuse: checked, confirmed nothing applicable\n\nNone of the ~113 Phase-7-restored `kotoba-lang` CLJC crates (`physics-2d`,\n`pathfind`, `tilemap`, etc.) expose anything the kami-clj **guest** compiler\ncan call — they're host-side-only Rust-callable libraries, not part of the\nguest module's fixed host-import vocabulary. The guest compiler's callable\nsurface is exactly the 14 host-imports `kami-script-runtime-rs` implements,\nmatching this session's established finding (concept 2/3/4/5 investigations\nfor isekai-network) that guest logic cannot reach Rust-substrate crates\ndirectly.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- The specific compile-and-run blocker `isekai-network`'s README documented\n  all session is closed — real execution, real pixel-verified rendering,\n  both backends deterministic.\n- `kotoba-lang/engine` now has both compile halves closed (semantic compile\n  + byte emission); the previously-undocumented host-runtime gap now has an\n  owning repo.\n- `kami-genre-base-systems` (a separate, parallel initiative this session)\n  can, as real follow-up, actually WASM-compile and run its systems through\n  this same pipeline — not attempted in this ADR's scope.\n- One naming question (`kami-script-runtime-rs`) is explicitly deferred,\n  not silently accepted as final.\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n\n1. **Wait for `kotoba-lang/kami-script-runtime`'s own scope to eventually\n   cover the host runtime**: rejected — that repo states the exclusion in\n   absolute, permanent terms.\n2. **Port the deleted Rust host runtime into `kami-engine`** (the\n   asset/contract shell repo): rejected — `kami-engine` runs a CI \"no-rust\n   guard,\" structurally cannot host Rust source.\n3. **Full `hecs`-based entity store instead of hand-rolled `HashMap`**:\n   rejected for this pass given this session's established slow-build cost\n   for wgpu/wasmtime-adjacent Rust crates — the hand-rolled store is real,\n   tested, and functionally equivalent for current verification needs;\n   `hecs` parity is a disclosed, legitimate follow-up.\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2607010930 (clj-wgsl migration — the source of the deletion this ADR\n  recovers from)\n- ADR-2607023200 (isekai-network standalone repo — the consumer this work\n  unblocks)\n- `kotoba-lang/engine` PR #1, PR #2 (both merged)\n- `kotoba-lang/kami-script-runtime-rs` (new repo)\n- `gftdcojp/isekai-network`", :adr/decision "{:byte_emission {:location \"kotoba-lang/engine, new namespace kotoba.engine-clj.wasm-bytes\", :method \"1:1 port of the deleted Rust codegen.rs::compile's section\\n            assembly (type/import/function/memory/global/export/code/data,\\n            same order, same cabi_realloc bump-allocator special case),\\n            recovered read-only from kami-engine's git history at the pin\\n            already used for codegen.cljc's own recovery\", :verification \"wasm-tools validate (independent external validator, not\\n                   self-consistency) on both a minimal example and\\n                   isekai-network's real logic.clj; wasmtime run --invoke\\n                   actually executing emitted bytes and returning the\\n                   correct value; 51 tests / 213 assertions\", :bug_found_and_fixed \"PR #2: :f32-const missing num/f32-bits conversion,\\n                          found by kami-script-runtime-rs's real tick-loop\\n                          execution (ghosts spawned via a def-bound constant\\n                          moved correctly; ghosts using an inline f32\\n                          literal in the same cond sat at a NaN position\\n                          forever) -- fixed with 2 new regression tests\\n                          decoding the emitted bytes back via an independent\\n                          ByteBuffer read\"}, :host_runtime {:new_repo {:path \"kotoba-lang/kami-script-runtime-rs\", :visibility :public, :naming_note \"no stronger established -rs-suffix convention\\n                             was found in kotoba-lang for \\\"thin Rust\\n                             substrate paired with an almost-same-named CLJC\\n                             sibling\\\" at the time this repo was created --\\n                             flagged, not resolved (see :naming_review below)\"}, :scope \"wasmtime (JIT) + wasmi (no-JIT/interpreted) dual backends, one\\n           binding codebase, 14 host-import implementations recovered 1:1\\n           from the deleted lib.rs, hand-rolled HashMap-based entity store\\n           (NOT hecs -- disclosed simplification, hecs recovery was not\\n           attempted), render/audio/physics host-imports NOT implemented\\n           because isekai-network's actual compiled module declares none\\n           (confirmed empirically via the parity test's clean run, not\\n           assumed) -- matches the original pre-deletion Rust's own no-op\\n           status for those bindings\", :verification \"wasmi/wasmtime parity test runs isekai-network's real\\n                   compiled module through both backends for 200 ticks,\\n                   asserts bit-for-bit identical position/velocity/tag/count\\n                   state -- the golden-frame determinism contract\\n                   ADR-2607010930's original kami-script-runtime design\\n                   called for\", :kami_clj_play_integration \"src/bin/kami_clj_play.rs reuses the deleted\\n                                original's wgpu rendering/shader/instanced-\\n                                sprite code, replaced its in-process\\n                                hecs+CLJ-compile Game struct with a thin\\n                                KamiHost wrapper loading a pre-compiled\\n                                game.wasm (disclosed architectural change --\\n                                the compiler is CLJC now, not callable from\\n                                Rust at runtime) plus a hand-rolled\\n                                scene.edn parser scoped to author.clj's\\n                                known flat output shape (disclosed\\n                                simplification, not a general EDN reader).\\n                                Confirmed running: real window, sustained\\n                                ~60fps for 720 frames, isekai-network's\\n                                game.wasm executing live (entity count 5->21\\n                                via spawn, beat-spark bonus firing), pixel-\\n                                level colour verification via a real\\n                                render-to-texture screenshot capture\\n                                (Shiro-hood white near-exact match; teal/lime\\n                                eye-accent colours consistent with the\\n                                shader's 0.35*halo glow-brightening + sRGB\\n                                encode once that two-step colour pipeline\\n                                was correctly accounted for -- documented as\\n                                a comment directly in the fragment shader\\n                                source so future verification work does not\\n                                repeat the naive-hex-comparison gap)\"}, :naming_review {:finding \"no established kotoba-lang naming convention was found for\\n             this exact \\\"Rust substrate host paired with an almost-same-\\n             named CLJC sibling repo\\\" shape at the time of creation --\\n             kami-script-runtime-rs's own README already flagged this\\n             explicitly\", :recommendation \"not acted on unilaterally -- renaming a live,\\n                     manifest-registered, actively-depended-on public repo\\n                     is a disruptive decision this ADR defers to the\\n                     project owner. If a convention is later established\\n                     (e.g. a -rs suffix pattern emerges from other Phase-4/7\\n                     migration landings), kami-script-runtime-rs is the\\n                     first known instance and a rename would need a\\n                     west.yml pin update + isekai-network build-doc update,\\n                     not a blocking concern today\"}, :genre_base_systems_naming {:finding \"kami-genre-base-systems' games/<genre>/ layout mirrors\\n             kami-clj-play/games/<name>/'s established convention exactly\\n             (author.clj+logic.clj+deps.edn+.gitignore per named game) --\\n             consistent, no naming gap found\", :future_question \"whether individual genre systems should eventually\\n                      become separate kami-app-{genre} crates per\\n                      ARCHITECTURE.md's stated per-game-crate convention is\\n                      a real open question, deliberately not resolved here\\n                      -- these are BASE/FOUNDATION systems (pre-crate-worthy\\n                      prototypes), not shipped games, so the kami-clj-play/\\n                      games/ precedent (which also holds prototype-tier\\n                      reference games, not crate-worthy products) is the\\n                      better-fitting precedent for this repo's current\\n                      maturity level\"}, :library_reuse_check {:finding \"none of the ~113 Phase-7-restored kotoba-lang CLJC crates\\n             (kotoba-lang/physics-2d, /pathfind, /tilemap, etc.) expose\\n             anything the kami-clj GUEST compiler can call -- they are\\n             host-side-only Rust-callable libraries (or CLJC ports thereof\\n             consumed by Rust hosts), not part of the guest module's fixed\\n             host-import vocabulary. Confirmed, not assumed: the guest\\n             compiler's callable surface is exactly the 14 host-imports\\n             kami-script-runtime-rs implements, nothing more, matching this\\n             session's established finding (concept 2/3/4/5 investigations)\\n             that guest logic cannot reach Rust-substrate crates directly\"}}", :db/id -1, :adr/problem "{:source \"session-long thread: isekai-network (gftdcojp/isekai-network,\\n            Ghost Hacker: Shiro & Pico) had a real, EDN-validated,\\n            proven-vocabulary-checked games/01-netsurvivors/logic.clj since\\n            early in the session, but no way to verify it actually ran --\\n            kami-engine-clj (the compiler CLAUDE.md documented) turned out\\n            to have been deleted upstream (kotoba-lang/kotoba PR #259) as\\n            part of ADR-2607010930's clj-wgsl migration, and its CLJC\\n            replacement (found under the differently-named kotoba-lang/engine)\\n            only produced a Module IR data structure, not loadable .wasm\\n            bytes -- and even with bytes, nothing existed to actually load\\n            and execute them with real host-import behaviour\", :investigated [\"kotoba.engine-clj/compile-file successfully compiled isekai-network's\\n    real logic.clj to a Module IR with all 8 expected functions, 14\\n    host-imports, correctly-evaluated constants -- confirmed via direct\\n    testing before any new code was written\" \"the Module IR's byte-emission gap was explicitly documented in\\n    kotoba-lang/engine's own README (\\\"a future host-adapter package is\\n    expected to do this\\\") -- not a surprise discovery, a known, scoped-out\\n    TODO\" \"the deleted Rust kami-script-runtime/src/lib.rs (2042 lines) was fully\\n    recoverable from kami-engine's git history at the same pinned SHA\\n    codegen.rs was recovered from, confirming both halves of the deleted\\n    Rust workspace share one recoverable snapshot\" \"kotoba-lang/kami-script-runtime's own README states the host-runtime\\n    exclusion in absolute terms (\\\"permanent scope exclusion, not a TODO\\\"),\\n    confirming no other repo was quietly planning to cover this -- a real\\n    gap, not a duplication risk (kotoba-lang/wasm-ui, kotoba-lang/webgpu,\\n    kotoba-lang/ui, kotoba-lang/webgl, kotoba-lang/gpu were all separately\\n    surveyed and confirmed unrelated: browser-only DOM/WebGPU UI substrate\\n    or empty Phase-4 scaffolds, none targeting native windowed wasmtime\\n    hosting)\"], :risk \"porting Rust->CLJC codegen semantics correctly does not guarantee\\n         the separate mechanical byte-emission step is correct -- WASM\\n         binary format bugs (wrong section order, wrong opcode, wrong\\n         immediate encoding) can be structurally valid (wasm-tools validate\\n         passes) while being semantically wrong, as PR #2's f32-const bug\\n         demonstrated concretely\"}", :adr/alternatives "[{:option \"wait for kotoba-lang/kami-script-runtime's own scope to\\n            eventually cover the host runtime, rather than creating a new\\n            repo\", :rejected_because \"that repo's README states the exclusion in absolute,\\n                       permanent terms -- waiting on a scope change that has\\n                       already been explicitly ruled out is not a real path\"} {:option \"port the deleted Rust host runtime into kami-engine (the\\n            asset/contract shell repo) instead of a new repo\", :rejected_because \"kami-engine runs a CI \\\"no-rust guard\\\" (confirmed via\\n                       its own CLAUDE.md) -- structurally cannot host Rust\\n                       source\"} {:option \"attempt a full hecs-based entity store instead of the\\n            hand-rolled HashMap store, to match the original more closely\", :rejected_because \"time-boxed given this session's established slow-\\n                       build cost for wgpu/wasmtime-adjacent Rust crates --\\n                       the hand-rolled store is real, tested, and\\n                       functionally equivalent for this session's\\n                       verification needs; hecs parity is a disclosed,\\n                       legitimate follow-up, not silently dropped\"}]", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607031700: kotoba-lang/engine WASM byte-emission + kotoba-lang/kami-script-runtime-rs (the recovered WASM host substrate)", :adr/source-format "edn"}]